{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Write batches of records in TraffluentCollector’s ingest format, for an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HTTPDestination"},{"type":"text","text":" to send,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and read them back into records on a server."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/collectorencoding"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"topicSections":[{"title":"Encoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatch"],"anchor":"Encoding-batches"},{"title":"Records left out","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorEncodingError"],"anchor":"Records-left-out"},{"title":"Decoding batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/DecodedCollectorBatch","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoderError","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/NotACollectorBatch"],"anchor":"Decoding-batches"},{"title":"Records that can’t be read","identifiers":["doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/UndecodedRecord","doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError"],"anchor":"Records-that-cant-be-read"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" is the ","type":"text"},{"code":"BatchEncoder","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" for a self-hosted TraffluentCollector’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST \/v1\/batches","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". Give it to an ","type":"text"},{"code":"HTTPDestination","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (module ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":") as its encoder,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and pass the collector’s API key to the destination as an ","type":"text"},{"code":"Authorization: Bearer","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" header field.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is JSON: one object per record, with the record’s identifier (which a redelivered record","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"keeps), the event’s name, its timestamp, whether it is redelivered, its properties and its context.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Properties are read from the event’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Encodable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" form, which ","type":"text"},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" derives, through the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"event’s schema in the ","type":"text"},{"code":"TrackingPlan","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" the encoder is made with. The context holds the standard","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"context keys the record has values for, its session and sample rate, and its trace context. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" value is written only while the record reveals it; once redacted, a ","type":"text"},{"code":"Sensitive","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"property is left out, and an array’s element, or a value inside a type the plan can’t map, is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"null","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record the encoder can’t write is left out and the rest of the batch is sent: one whose event and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"version the plan doesn’t describe, one whose event isn’t "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Encodable"},{"type":"text","text":", one holding a value"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"JSON can’t, such as a NaN, and one whose timestamp has no ISO 8601 form (NaN, infinite, or more"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"than "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Int64.max"},{"type":"text","text":" milliseconds from 1970). "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/requests(for:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns each record left out"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"as a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SkippedRecord"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"},{"type":"text","text":"), which the destination logs and reports on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"dropReports"},{"type":"text","text":". When no record of a batch can be written, the destination sends nothing."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchEncoder\/batch(of:)"},{"type":"text","text":" returns the same body and skipped records without a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"destination."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To send to a server of your own format, write a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" of your own. To send to PostHog,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogBatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" (module "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PostHogEncoding"},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import CollectorEncoding","import HTTPDestinations","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let encoder = CollectorBatchEncoder(plan: plan)","let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,  \/\/ https:\/\/collector.example.com\/v1\/batches","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(apiKey)\"],","    encoder: encoder)","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/choosingdestinations","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers sending to the collector beside the other destinations.","type":"text"}]},{"level":3,"text":"Reading batches back","type":"heading","anchor":"Reading-batches-back"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" reads a body the encoder wrote back into "},{"code":"EventRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s, for a server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that receives an app’s batches and hands them to another destination, such as a relay in front"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of Google Analytics. Make it with the plan the app’s encoder was made with. It finds each record’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"event type by name among the "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"s the server links, or among the types you list"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorBatchDecoder\/init(plan:events:instrument:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import CollectorEncoding","import TrackingPlans","","let plan = try TrackingPlan()","let decoder = try CollectorBatchDecoder(plan: plan)","let batch = try decoder.batch(from: body)  \/\/ a body CollectorBatchEncoder wrote","await destination.receive(batch.records)"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each record keeps its identifier, timestamp (to the millisecond), event, redelivery flag and the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"context the body holds: its session’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"SessionKey"},{"type":"text","text":", its sample rate, the standard context and its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"trace context, which the decoder’s instrument extracts. Encoding the records again with an encoder"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of the same plan writes the same bytes. A record the decoder can’t read is left out and the rest"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are read: one of an event it has no type of, or whose type’s version the plan doesn’t describe, one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"missing a member or holding what the encoder never writes, and one with a property the event’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type can’t read: a required "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" property a delivery redacted, an array of non-optional"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"type":"text","text":" elements it redacted, or an integer outside its property’s type."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body names each record’s event but not its version, so a record is read at the version of the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"decoder’s type of that name. Deploy the server with the event types the apps send. Once an event’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"version is raised, a record from an app still at the earlier version is read as the newer one:","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported as ","type":"text"},{"code":"undecodableProperty","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" when its properties don’t fit the newer type, and read as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"newer version when they do.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/DecodedCollectorBatch\/undecodedRecords"},{"text":" holds a report of each, an ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/UndecodedRecord"},{"text":" whose","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reason is a ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/CollectorDecodingError"},{"text":". A body that isn’t a collector batch at all throws","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/CollectorEncoding\/documentation\/CollectorEncoding\/NotACollectorBatch"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]}],"metadata":{"roleHeading":"Framework","role":"collection","title":"CollectorEncoding","modules":[{"name":"CollectorEncoding"}],"externalID":"CollectorEncoding","symbolKind":"module"},"kind":"symbol","references":{"doc://HTTPDestinations/documentation/HTTPDestinations":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"text":"Send each batch of records to an HTTP endpoint, and send it again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"title":"HTTPDestinations","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations","url":"\/documentation\/httpdestinations","role":"collection","kind":"symbol"},"doc://CollectorEncoding/documentation/Coll